WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.930
Your client tracker, your follow-up rhythm, and client feedback.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.660
This is the video for module 2 of Client Relationship Management.

3
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:22.470
Make a spreadsheet called Client tracker with two tabs. Clients has one row per person, with her details and next action. Orders has one row per order, so Sheets can add up her history for you.

4
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:36.480
Add drop-down lists, so a status is always written the same way: New, Active, Quiet or Lapsed. Link the client names in Orders to the client list, so every name is spelled exactly the same.

5
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:42.910
COUNTIF counts how many orders each client has made. SUMIF adds up what she has spent.

6
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:53.290
Then use conditional formatting so any client whose next action date has passed turns red. Each morning, the red rows are your follow-up list.

7
00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:01.460
Keep the sheet private. Share it with no one, or only a trusted staff member, so client phone numbers stay safe.

8
00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:06.400
Test your formulas once with a calculator, so you can trust them.

9
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:16.910
Ngozi's Orders tab shows 4 orders for Ifeoma: 18,000, 22,000, 18,000 and 25,000 naira.

10
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.800
That adds up to 83,000 naira, the same as the sheet.

11
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:34.440
But one order had been typed as Ifeoma with an extra space, and the count missed it. That is exactly why drop-down lists matter. Also type amounts as plain numbers, without the naira sign.

12
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:45.120
Many problems start before delivery, when the client and the business understood different things. One thought Friday meant morning. The other meant evening.

13
00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:53.840
So once she agrees, send a short WhatsApp confirmation covering these five points, and ask her to reply confirmed.

14
00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.840
Save it as a quick reply, and change the details each time.

15
00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:05.850
Send a confirmation on day 0, a progress update before delivery, and a handover note on delivery day.

16
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:14.590
On day 3, send a short after-care check. I hope the trays went well at the meeting. Was the quantity right for your guests?

17
00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.740
And remind her when she is likely to need you again.

18
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:26.320
Do not crowd her. Between orders, send no more than one non-sales message a month, unless she starts the conversation.

19
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:36.760
For example, Funmi supplies liquid soap to Halima's provisions shop. Halima ordered on 3 February, 1 March, 4 April and 2 May.

20
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.980
From her first order to her last is 88 days.

21
00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:49.590
4 orders means 3 gaps. 88 divided by 3 is about 29 days. That is her reorder gap.

22
00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:58.140
So Funmi messages on 28 May: your last delivery was 2 May. Shall I bring the usual 6 kegs on Friday?

23
00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.750
Halima is reminded before she runs out, so she does not buy elsewhere.

24
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:11.510
Clients rarely announce that they are leaving. A healthy relationship looks like steady orders, replies and referrals.

25
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:26.590
Warning signs are longer gaps, smaller orders and unanswered messages. One sign may mean nothing. Two or more are worth a gentle, honest check-in. Do not guilt her. Ask whether your service still fits her needs.

26
00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:35.200
Ask 2 or 3 short questions, including: on a scale of 0 to 10, how likely are you to recommend me to a friend?

27
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:44.480
For example, Ruth tutors pupils in Lagos and asks 20 parents. 12 answer 9 or 10. They are promoters, 60 percent.

28
00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:49.470
5 answer 7 or 8. They are passives, and are left out.

29
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:58.500
3 answer 6 or lower. They are detractors, 15 percent. Her score is 60 minus 15, which is 45.

30
00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:07.090
More useful still, two detractors said lesson times changed without notice. So Ruth now gives a week's notice of any change.

31
00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:20.390
To remember. Keep one row per client and one per order. Confirm every order in writing. Before you mark an order as Paid, check your bank app, because a screenshot is not proof of payment.

32
00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:27.380
Time reminders from her own reorder gap. And when a client gives feedback, change one thing and tell her you did.

33
00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:44.650
Now practise. Build your tracker with at least 10 real clients and test one total by hand. Save your confirmation as a quick reply and work out three reorder gaps. Then send the feedback questions to five clients and calculate your score.

34
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.940
Continue with the lessons below.
